docs/en/device_dev_guide/driver/bus_driver/PCI/pci_host.md:109:- **Switch:** Provides expansion or aggregation capabilities, allowing more devices to connect to a single PCIe port. They act as packet routers, identifying which path a given packet should take based on its address or other routing information. A switch is a type of PCIe-to-PCIe bridge.
docs/en/device_dev_guide/driver/bus_driver/PCI/pci_host.md:111:- **Endpoint (EP):** An EP is a device at the leaf of the PCIe topology and is the ultimate initiator or completer of I/O operations. Examples include PCIe network cards and NVMe SSDs. An Endpoint can only accept packets from an upstream component or send packets to an upstream component.
